// Sandbox control plane.
//
// A sandbox is a short-lived, strongly-isolated microVM bound to a single
// workload (function, task, or container). Unlike MachineService VMs, a
// sandbox is decoupled from its workload: an execution exiting does NOT
// destroy the sandbox — it transitions back to READY and continues accepting
// executions until an explicit Stop/Remove or TTL expiry.
//
// This file is the **control plane**: creating, inspecting, listing, and
// destroying sandboxes, plus their lifecycle events and published ports.
// These calls address a fleet — in cloud deployments they are served by a
// multi-tenant front door that knows which node holds which sandbox.
//
